sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title Workflow 1: Static file request (FIFO) - the main critical path
    participant C as Client
    participant M as Master thread
    participant Q as Shared request buffer<br/>(mutex + not_empty / not_full)
    participant W as Worker thread
    participant FS as File system
    participant S as Stats recorder

    C->>M: TCP connect + "GET /index.html HTTP/1.0"
    M->>M: accept() returns conn_fd, stamp t_arrive
    M->>Q: lock(mutex)
    M->>Q: put(conn_fd, t_arrive), count++
    M->>Q: signal(not_empty), unlock(mutex)
    Note over M: Master goes straight back to accept()<br/>and never reads the request itself (FIFO)

    W->>Q: lock(mutex)
    Note over W,Q: while count == 0: wait(not_empty, mutex)
    Q-->>W: woken, get() oldest request, count--
    W->>Q: signal(not_full), unlock(mutex)
    W->>W: stamp t_dequeue
    W->>C: read request line and headers
    W->>FS: stat(path), check it stays under basedir
    FS-->>W: file size and permissions
    W->>FS: open() and read() file
    FS-->>W: file contents
    W->>C: write "HTTP/1.0 200 OK" + headers + body
    W->>C: close(conn_fd)
    W->>S: lock(stats), append t_arrive, t_dequeue, t_done, unlock(stats)
    Note over W: Worker loops back and waits on not_empty again
